WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.435
Hi, I'm Nick Gillespie, an editor at

00:00:01.436 --> 00:00:02.577
large at Reason, your

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:04.920
source since 1968 for

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:08.279
everything related to free minds and

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.719
free markets.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.829
We're in the middle of Reason's

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.239
annual webathon.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.069
The one time, each year, we ask

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.779
our online readers, viewers and

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.639
listeners to support our

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.459
principled libertarian journalism.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.000
We're trying to pull in $400,000 in new donations. 

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.069
Your gifts are tax deductible

00:00:26.069 --> 00:00:28.018
and go directly to funding our print

00:00:28.018 --> 00:00:30.147
journalism, our video productions

00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:31.856
and our podcasts.

00:00:31.856 --> 00:00:33.835
What's more? They're being matched.

00:00:33.835 --> 00:00:35.844
So every dollar you give

00:00:35.844 --> 00:00:37.643
goes twice as far.

00:00:37.643 --> 00:00:39.922
If you like what we've been doing

00:00:39.922 --> 00:00:41.631
and what we're going to keep doing,

00:00:41.631 --> 00:00:42.900
please give now.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.850
Go to reason.com/donate. For

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.085
giving levels and associated swags,

00:00:48.085 --> 00:00:49.991
some of it's pretty great.

00:00:49.991 --> 00:00:51.389
And from all of my colleagues,

00:00:51.389 --> 00:00:52.389
thanks!

